\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Cost of {$\mathbb  {B}\text  {it}\mathbb  {Z}$}\ (\cref  {c:core_iop}) for committing to $\ell = 2^{n}$ bits, $n = 20, \ldots  , 30$, and proving one claim $\langle \mathbf  {v}, \mathbf  {f}\rangle = \mu $ over $\ensuremath  {\mathbb  {F}}_q$ for a prime $q$ sampled uniformly (after the commitment) from $[2^{b-1}, 2^{b})$, $b = \min (113, 127 - \log \ell _1 - W)$ at cell width $W = 1$ ($b = 108, \ldots  , 113$), $\mathbf  {v}= \mathsf  {eq}(\cdot , \ensuremath  {\mathbf  {r}}_1) \otimes \mathsf  {eq}(\cdot , \ensuremath  {\mathbf  {r}}_2)$ with $(\ensuremath  {\mathbf  {r}}_1, \ensuremath  {\mathbf  {r}}_2)$ sampled after $q$, and the tensor split $\ell _1 = 2^{\lceil 0.6\, n\rceil }$, $\ell _1 \cdot \ell _2 = \ell $ (\cref  {s:instantiation}). The commitment is opened with ring switching and Ligerito~\cite  {ligerito} over a Reed--Solomon code of rate $1/8$ over $\ensuremath  {\mathbb  {F}}_{2^{128}}$ (initial folding of $2^{4}$ rows, Johnson regime, BLAKE3 Merkle trees), configured for $100$ bits of round-by-round security (the minimum over its levels and error terms is $100.0$ bits); Round 0 (the out-of-domain sample) is executed with $\lceil \log \ell - 23.7 \rceil $ bits of grinding ($0$ to $7$ over the table); every other round (the GKR, the sumcheck reducing to MLE evaluation claims, the ring switch) has error at most $7 \cdot 2^{-128}$. Prover columns: \emph  {commit} is the commitment to the $\ell $ bits; \emph  {grand products} is computing the integers $\mu _j$ and the batched GKR for the $\ell _2$ grand products in the exponent (\cref  {s:gkr_low_entropy}); \emph  {ring switch} is the sumcheck reducing the GKR output claims to MLE evaluation claims together with the ring-switching step; \emph  {Ligerito} is the Ligerito opening; \emph  {total} is the commitment plus the end-to-end proving time (each entry is a median, so the parts need not add up exactly). \emph  {Non-Ligerito} proof bytes are the $\mu _j$, the GKR and sumcheck messages, and the ring-switch message; KB $= 1000$ bytes. Apple M4 (10 cores: 4 performance + 6 efficiency), 16\,GB, 8 threads; medians of 5 runs after one warm-up.}}{56}{table.caption.59}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:f2z-raw-performance}{{11}{56}{Cost of \ftwoz \ (\cref {c:core_iop}) for committing to $\codedim = 2^{n}$ bits, $n = 20, \ldots , 30$, and proving one claim $\langle \vv , \bff \rangle = \mu $ over $\FF _q$ for a prime $q$ sampled uniformly (after the commitment) from $[2^{b-1}, 2^{b})$, $b = \min (113, 127 - \log \codedim _1 - W)$ at cell width $W = 1$ ($b = 108, \ldots , 113$), $\vv = \eq (\cdot , \rr _1) \otimes \eq (\cdot , \rr _2)$ with $(\rr _1, \rr _2)$ sampled after $q$, and the tensor split $\codedim _1 = 2^{\lceil 0.6\, n\rceil }$, $\codedim _1 \cdot \codedim _2 = \codedim $ (\cref {s:instantiation}). The commitment is opened with ring switching and Ligerito~\cite {ligerito} over a Reed--Solomon code of rate $1/8$ over $\FF _{2^{128}}$ (initial folding of $2^{4}$ rows, Johnson regime, BLAKE3 Merkle trees), configured for $100$ bits of round-by-round security (the minimum over its levels and error terms is $100.0$ bits); Round 0 (the out-of-domain sample) is executed with $\lceil \log \codedim - 23.7 \rceil $ bits of grinding ($0$ to $7$ over the table); every other round (the GKR, the sumcheck reducing to MLE evaluation claims, the ring switch) has error at most $7 \cdot 2^{-128}$. Prover columns: \emph {commit} is the commitment to the $\codedim $ bits; \emph {grand products} is computing the integers $\mu _j$ and the batched GKR for the $\codedim _2$ grand products in the exponent (\cref {s:gkr_low_entropy}); \emph {ring switch} is the sumcheck reducing the GKR output claims to MLE evaluation claims together with the ring-switching step; \emph {Ligerito} is the Ligerito opening; \emph {total} is the commitment plus the end-to-end proving time (each entry is a median, so the parts need not add up exactly). \emph {Non-Ligerito} proof bytes are the $\mu _j$, the GKR and sumcheck messages, and the ring-switch message; KB $= 1000$ bytes. Apple M4 (10 cores: 4 performance + 6 efficiency), 16\,GB, 8 threads; medians of 5 runs after one warm-up}{table.caption.59}{}}
\newlabel{tab:f2z-raw-performance@cref}{{[table][11][]11}{[1][56][]56}{}{}{}}
